    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good high-level view, but some critics say that \"balancing\" is just a way to delay necessary action. they argue that if we don't prioritize the phase-out immediately, the long-term cost of climate catastrophe will far outweigh any short-term economic pain. from a policy standpoint, is it actually realistic to treat economic stability and decarbonization as equal priorities, or is the environmental threat so existential that the economic risks should be viewed as secondary?",
